Q("The customer pushes back on a submitted quotation. The change is made by:", ["Editing the submitted document", "Cancel then Amend — v2 carries the history", "A fresh quotation ignoring v1", "A phone agreement"], 1, "Amendments keep the negotiation readable as v1 → v2.", "Ch6"),
Q("An Open offer with no response after the third chase should be:", ["Kept Open to flatter the pipeline", "Marked Lost with reason 'no response'", "Deleted", "Re-submitted"], 1, "An Open list you can trust beats a big fake one.", "Ch6, Ch7"),
Q("Auto-expiry of quotations protects the seller by:", ["Punishing slow customers", "Preventing acceptance at stale prices — refresh happens by design", "Reducing database size", "Hiding old offers"], 1, "Expired offers force a repriced conversation politely, in advance.", "Ch6"),
Q("A lost-reason taxonomy that works is:", ["Twenty precise categories", "Short and honest — Price, Competitor, Timing, No budget, Spec, No response", "A free-text field", "Optional"], 1, "Reps must pick truthfully in seconds for the data to compound.", "Ch7"),
